# Line endings
#
# The bundled web app must stay byte-identical to what moddys.net serves, so git must not
# rewrite line endings inside it: a newline inside a JS template literal is content, and
# byte-identity is what makes hash comparisons against the live site meaningful. The same goes
# for the shim, which is byte-identical to the Android app's copy.
# `**` so the nested maplibre/ engine and glyphs are covered too, not just the top level.
Resources/www/** -text

# Source files: normalise to LF in the repository (checked out per platform default).
*.swift text
*.yml text
*.md text
*.py text

# tools/shim_harness.py is pinned by BYTES in SHIM.sha256 and checked in CI, so it needs the
# same LF bytes on every platform (a Windows checkout used to hand the check a CRLF copy the
# recorded hash could never match).
tools/shim_harness.py text eol=lf
